# EVERY LAYER WHOSE OWN TWO MEASUREMENTS IMPLY DEMAND THAT COULD HAVE GONE UNSERVED, BESIDE
# WHETHER ANYBODY CAN SAY WHAT HAPPENED TO IT. One row per exposed layer, in exactly one of
# three standings.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE THREE BUFFERS ARE SUBSTITUTES, SO THE QUESTION IS ASKED OF THE ROW AND NEVER OF ONE
#    COLUMN. An excess above the nameplate can be absorbed by running hot, by drawing on stock,
#    or by making the demand wait. A layer whose capacity buffer is empty has ONE route closed,
#    which is not the same fact as having nowhere to go, and the two were the same fact here
#    until this relation existed.
#
#      a buffer nobody sized          SUSPENDED. One route is unmeasured, so the ceiling is
#                                     unknown and no conclusion about it is available. An
#                                     excess the filer says was absorbed by running hot is
#                                     not contradicted by an empty stock room.
#      a buffer with room in it       The exposure had somewhere to go. Nothing is owed.
#      every buffer sized and empty   Every route accounted for, none with room. The demand
#                                     above the nameplate had nowhere to go, so somebody
#                                     went without and somebody has to be named.
#
# ⛔⛔ ONLY THE THIRD LICENSES A RULE, AND SAYING SO IS THE WHOLE POINT OF CLASSIFYING THE OTHER
#    TWO RATHER THAN FILTERING THEM AWAY. A suspended layer and a satisfied layer are the same
#    row to a `WHERE`, and they are opposite facts: one says the filing is fine, the other says
#    nobody looked. algebra/exposure_standing.sqlc holds the three to a partition so a layer
#    cannot fall out of all of them and quietly shrink the population.
#
# ⛔ THE ORDER OF THE ARMS IS THE PRECEDENCE AND IT IS DELIBERATE. Ignorance outranks room: a
#   layer with stock to spare AND an unmeasured queue is SUSPENDED, because the spare stock
#   does not tell you whether the queue held anything.
-- layers/remainder.sqlc where exposure > 0, classified by layers/absorption.sqlc.
SELECT r.*, a.absorbable, a.unknown,
       CASE WHEN a.unknown    > 0 THEN 'a buffer nobody sized'
            WHEN a.absorbable > 0 THEN 'a buffer with room in it'
            ELSE                       'every buffer sized and empty' END AS standing
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
) r
JOIN      (
    :compose(layers/absorption.sqlc)
) a USING (filing, layer)
WHERE r.exposure > 1e-9
